From f9a61e8074b16501b8be0550fdcefd9081bf8760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Bayer <roba@itu.dk>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 22:32:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add AMCBandwidth listener: Apple-silicon DRAM bandwidth via
 IOReport

New listener (enable with RADT_LISTENER_AMCBANDWIDTH=True) that streams
per-engine memory-controller bandwidth as radt metrics:

  system/amc - {Cpu|Gpu|Ane|Other} {Rd|Wr} GBps
  system/amc - Total GBps

It runs an external clang-compiled sampler binary that reads the Apple
Memory Controller's per-requestor DRAM byte counters from the private
IOReport framework (no root required), parses its per-interval CSV
stream (default 0.5 s cadence), and pushes metrics through the batched
listener logger like the top listener does. The binary is located via
env CHOREO_AMC_SAMPLER_BIN or PATH; it stays external because the
IOReport calls need Objective-C blocks and an ABI where
IOReportSimpleGetIntegerValue's 2nd argument must be NULL.

On non-Darwin platforms, a missing binary, or a machine whose IOReport
exposes no AMC channels, the listener prints one warning and exits
cleanly instead of crashing the run. SIGTERM (how RADTBenchmark stops
listeners) is forwarded to the sampler so it is never orphaned.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
